    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=start&amp;rev=1745733593&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-27T05:59:53+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>admin (admin@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>start</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=start&amp;rev=1745733593&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agents for Insolvency &amp; Bankruptcy (IBC2016)

----------

communication_agents
  COMMUNICATION AGENTS  Generative chatbots serve as a communication platform where stakeholders can seek answers to their queries regarding the insolvency process. These chatbots provide instant responses, helping to manage stakeholder expectations and reduce the workload of IPs by addressing routine inquiries.</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agentic_framework:process_agents&amp;rev=1745655370&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-26T08:16:10+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>admin (admin@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>process_agents</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=agentic_framework:process_agents&amp;rev=1745655370&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Process Agents

Process agents can be categorized into distinct groups based on their roles and functionalities, offering specialized capabilities to enhance efficiency, accuracy, and decision-making in insolvency processes. These categories include Legal Agents, Process Agents, Planning Agents, Marketing Agents, Fraud Detection Agents, and Prediction Agents. Each type of agent addresses specific challenges within the insolvency framework, streamlining operations and improving outcomes. Process …</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=stakeholders:claimant_creditors&amp;rev=1745655149&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-26T08:12:29+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>admin (admin@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>claimant_creditors</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=stakeholders:claimant_creditors&amp;rev=1745655149&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agentic Services for Claimants

CLAIMANTS - Creditor claimants are individuals or entities with financial claims against the corporate debtor. They include financial creditors, operational creditors, and secured creditors, each with distinct rights under the IBC framework. Their claims are verified and prioritized during CIRP to ensure equitable distribution of recovered assets. Claimants play a pivotal role in guiding creditors through the claim submission, verification, and status tracking pro…</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=stakeholders:committee_creditors&amp;rev=1745655140&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-26T08:12:20+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>admin (admin@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>committee_creditors</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=stakeholders:committee_creditors&amp;rev=1745655140&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agentic Services for Committee of Creditors

CREDITOR COMMITTEES - The Committee of Creditors (CoC) is formed by financial creditors and plays a pivotal role in CIRP. It evaluates resolution plans, monitors the insolvency professional’s actions, and ensures decisions align with value maximization and fairness. The CoC serves as the final authority on accepting or rejecting resolution plans. Committee of Creditors plays a central role in the insolvency resolution process, and AI-driven agents can…</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=stakeholders:corporate_debtors&amp;rev=1745655131&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-26T08:12:11+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>admin (admin@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>corporate_debtors</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=stakeholders:corporate_debtors&amp;rev=1745655131&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agentic Services for Debtors

CORPORATE DEBTORS - Corporate debtors are entities that have defaulted on their financial obligations, triggering insolvency proceedings under the IBC. They are central to the resolution process, as their assets and operations are managed to maximize value for creditors. During the Corporate Insolvency Resolution Process (CIRP), control shifts from the corporate debtor&#039;s management to insolvency professionals. Corporate Debtors can benefit significantly from special…</description>
    </item>
    <item rdf:about="https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=stakeholders:forensic_auditors&amp;rev=1745655121&amp;do=diff">
        <dc:format>text/html</dc:format>
        <dc:date>2025-04-26T08:12:01+00:00</dc:date>
        <dc:creator>admin (admin@undisclosed.example.com)</dc:creator>
        <title>forensic_auditors</title>
        <link>https://resolutionbazaar.com/doku.php?id=stakeholders:forensic_auditors&amp;rev=1745655121&amp;do=diff</link>
        <description>Agentic Services for Auditors

FORENSIC AUDITORS - Forensic auditors investigate financial irregularities and fraudulent transactions within the corporate debtor’s accounts. Their findings help insolvency professionals and creditor committees identify potential recoverable assets and assess compliance with legal norms. Forensic Auditors Forensic Auditors play a critical role in insolvency proceedings by automating the extraction and analysis of financial data from company records. Their primary …</description>
    </item>
